# Codebase second brain

_Auto-synced: 2026-06-04T21:16:30.603344+00:00_
_Regenerate: `python scripts/codebase_brain.py sync`_

## Problem & goal

Tutorial videos go stale when the product UI changes. Goal: preserve
high-quality edited tutorials and minimize manual re-editing by diffing
old vs new screen recordings and transferring edit intent.

Full product spec: `plan.mb`.

## Pipeline (plan.mb → code)

| Step | Status | Where in code |
|------|--------|---------------|
| 1a Cut / transition detection | [x] done | video_segmentation/segmentation.py — detect_scenes (PySceneDetect) |
| 1b Workflow section chunking + narration alignment | [~] partial | timeline.py + transcription.align_to_segments; no LLM workflow labels |
| 1c Edited regions (zoom, crop, highlight, cursor focus) | [ ] planned | Not started — edit metadata on timeline |
| 2 UI element targets (cursor, narration, zoom, overlays) | [~] partial | OCR ui_elements + transcript; no cursor/zoom/highlight geometry |
| 3 Locate equivalent elements in new UI / video | [ ] planned | Needs old/new comparison pipeline |
| 4 Semantic UI diffing (layout, rename, feature changes) | [ ] planned | OpenCV diff + LLM + optional DOM — not implemented |
| 5 Editing intent transfer (re-anchor zoom/highlight/crop) | [ ] planned | Editing Intent Transfer Engine |
| 6 Merge updated segments + voice clone | [ ] planned | Timeline merge + TTS — not implemented |
| 7 Export to Akool / editable project data | [ ] planned | timeline.json only; no Akool/MCP export yet |

